# Keep every file byte-identical between the working copy, what git stores,
# and what raw.githubusercontent.com serves.
#
# This is not a style preference. The updater verifies each downloaded file
# against a SHA-256 recorded in manifest.json, and that manifest is generated
# by hashing the working copy. With git converting line endings on checkout,
# the working copy was CRLF while GitHub served LF — different bytes, so every
# text file failed its checksum and no install could ever update itself.
#
# "-text" tells git to leave line endings exactly as they are, in both
# directions, so the three copies can never drift apart again.
* -text
